   "subject": "Re: `fill` scale of `geom_point` is not shown in the legend",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">P.S. thank you for the solution with override.aes  - it&#39;s exactly what I was advised on stackoverflow at the end, and the only working solution so far.</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Monday, December 1, 2014 5:21:26 PM UTC-5, Vasily A. wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Ista, could you please explain - why it &quot;doesn&#39;t have fill&quot; while we see on the figure that the color really corresponds to color defined by `scale_fill_manual` - what is it, if not a fill?<br><br><br><br>On Monday, December 1, 2014 11:23:05 AM UTC-5, Ista Zahn wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">The geom used in the legend is a solid point, so it doesn&#39;t have a fill. You can force it to use another symbol, like this:<br><br>ggplot(data=df, mapping = aes(x=xx, y=yy)) +<br>  geom_point(aes(shape=type3, fill=type2), size=5) +<br>  scale_shape_manual(values=c(24,25,21)) +<br>  scale_fill_manual( values=c(&#39;green&#39;, &#39;red&#39;)) +<br>  guides(fill = guide_legend(override.aes = list(shape = 21)))<br><br><br></div><div style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">Best,<br>Ista<br></div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Dec 1, 2014 at 12:42 AM, Vasily A. <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">fgkldkgk...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"http://i.stack.imgur.com/O3aIC.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://i.stack.imgur.com/O3aIC.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369860699000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_RNA8-VjSPRH4F5wY8hYG\"><img height=\"133\" width=\"320\" border=\"0\"></a></p>My sample code is as following:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                 type2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;a&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;b&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;a&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;a&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;b&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;b&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">                 </span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code>type3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;A&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;C&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;B&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;A&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;B&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;C&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mapping </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shape</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">type3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">type2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  scale_shape_manual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">values</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">24</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">25</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">21</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  scale_fill_manual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> values</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;green&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;red&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Resulting plot has a legend but it&#39;s &#39;type2&#39; section doesn&#39;t reflect scale of <code>fill</code> value.<br>I <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/27221011/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/27221011/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369860699000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Qo41D-xt2Ix_742G4C6hd\">asked on Stackoverflow and was suggested a workaround</a> which works by drawing one more layer of points, but I still don&#39;t understand why the scale is not shown natively, so I would really appreciate authors&#39; comments.<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibi